      "writtenOn": "2023-10-17T07:14:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes and no.\nNSS#notifyNetworkStatus has to be a synchronize call from CS.\nThis is to stop CS/Netd from changing any network related information before NSS can collect the numbers.\nIn other words, these variable has to be accessed both from binder thread (CS-\u003enotifyNetworkStatus) and the handler thread (MSG_NOTIFY_NETWORK_STATUS) for now.\nThus, the lock cannot be removed.\n\nIn long-term, there is a plan to remove the need of synchonization between CS \u003c-\u003e NSS, which is documented here:\nhttps://docs.google.com/document/d/1zbVZZkS26JtbnQ2srn3BzKo1lF6uVoyFQwFGYIiiKpU/edit?resourcekey\u003d0-MQ5SR8e9trJegBMn6u6aag#heading\u003dh.l855nuu3svpz\nAfter the plan is done, we might be able to remove some of the locks.\nReopen if any idea.",
